  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+bx \\\\ -6x+cy\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $c+b?$",
  "worked_solution": "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ -x+3y \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y-x \\\\ -6x+7y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}5x+4y \\\\ 3y+(-1)x \\\\ -6x+(7)y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $c+b=(-1)+7=6.$",
